# IE-05 primary-source and later-result check

Checked on 11 September 2026.

- [Peca-Medlin, version 2](https://arxiv.org/html/2308.16146v2): Section 1.2 for partial-pivoting and QR conventions; Section 3.2 and Appendix B for the conjecture. The independent mathematical review records the exact distinction between the finite-order ratio and the asymptotic question.
- [Current arXiv record](https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.16146): latest revision remains v2, dated 16 April 2024.
- [SIAM publication record](https://epubs.siam.org/doi/full/10.1137/23M1597733): SIAM Journal on Matrix Analysis and Applications 45(3), 1599-1620 (2024), DOI 10.1137/23M1597733.

Bounded web searches for `"orthogonal" "Peca-Medlin" "conjecture" counterexample` and `"Growth factors of orthogonal matrices" extremizer 2026` located the primary paper and related growth literature, without a full resolution of the canonical equality. The 2026 butterfly results found by the search concern a different structured family and pivoting question. No search result is used as mathematical evidence for the new counterexample. The public-fork/branch audit is recorded separately in [network-check.json](network-check.json); neither check asserts exhaustive historical priority.

